  "_meta": {
    "status": "HARVESTED — recipe classification for Essence Crafting effects.",
    "note": "The bridge between the two vocabularies inside essence_crafting.json. `placements` is keyed by EFFECT NAME (157); `values_by_ml` is keyed by CURVE ROW (75), a coarser family vocabulary. Neither table states the join. table_2c ('Recipes for scaling effects') supplies it for the family rows by carrying a GROUP column, and table_2b ('Recipes for non-scaling effects') supplies the other half: an effect listed there does not scale, so having no ML curve is CORRECT for it rather than a gap.",
    "sources": {
      "scaling_groups": "https://ddowiki.com/page/Essence_Crafting/table_2c",
      "non_scaling": "https://ddowiki.com/page/Essence_Crafting/table_2b"
    },
    "harvested": "2026-08-29",
    "caveats": "Names here are table_2c's, verbatim, and they do NOT all match `placements` names: table_2c says 'Dodge Bonus' where placements says 'Dodge', and 'Armor-piercing' where placements says 'Armor-Piercing'. Normalisation is the JOIN's job (src/essence_curve_join.py), not this shard's — keeping the raw value means a re-reading never needs a re-harvest.\n\nThe 'Missing' group is the wiki's own: four recipes it marks 'not exist at all'. They are kept verbatim so the join can refuse them loudly rather than silently finding no row.\n\n107 further table_2c rows carry an EMPTY group and cost 400/1000 rather than 10/15. They are the named shard adjectives ('Airwarded', 'Anchored', \"Arcanist's\"), a third vocabulary, and are deliberately not harvested here."
  },
